@LINVM_SELFHOST{version=1 purpose=linvm_selfhosted_interpreter_all_33_opcodes scope=phase1 emits=LIN ops=33 sels=32 sweep_sels=88}
// P1: LinVM self-hosted interpreter - all 33 VmOp opcodes, i64 wrapping,
// deterministic trace fold (opcode, sp_after), VM_STEP_LIMIT, sp_at_ret,
// VmError status codes. General multi-slot array pool (up to 8 slots over
// a flat 256-cell pool; slot ids in loc[], lens in loc[56..63]) mirroring
// compiler/lin.zig vmExec (pool [VM_MAX_ARRS][VM_MAX_ARR_LEN]i64).
// Embedded programs: corpus subset (bithacks/crypto/compat/map/array_kernel)
// + hand-assembled 33-opcode coverage vectors. Bytecode tables generated by
// a transcription of compiler/lin.zig vmTokenize+VmComp (see docs).

// -------- flat module bytecode tables (generated; see docs/P1_LINVM_SELFHOST.rulel) --------
// fn table: 4 words per fn
//   ft[4*i]   = nparams | (start << 6)
//   ft[4*i+1] = len | (narrs << 10)
//   ft[4*i+2] = array pairs 0..3: (li | arrn << 6) << (15*s)
//   ft[4*i+3] = array pairs 4..7
// arrays are assigned slots in LOCAL order (Zig pool_used order); loc[li] holds
// the slot id; plen for slot s lives in loc[56+s]; pool is flat 256 cells with
// per-slot base = sum of previous lens (Zig: [8][256]i64, LIN cap: 256 cells).

// -------- interpreter core (port of vmExec, all 33 VmOp) --------
// modes: 0=value 1=subtree steps 2=status 3=trace-fold 4=sp_at_ret
// status codes: 0=ok 1=VmStepLimit 2=VmStackOverflow 3=VmStackUnderflow
//               4=VmBadFunction 5=VmDepth 6=VmArity 7=VmDivisionByZero
// trace fold (per completed instruction, execution order, i64 wrapping):
//   h = ((h + opcode) * 31) + sp_after
!vms_core(sel: int, fn_idx: int, depth: int, steps_in: int, mode: int, h_in: int, x0: int, x1: int, x2: int, x3: int): int {
